{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/991659-animal-wraiths","id":991659,"title":"Animal wraiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-22T19:24:07-07:00","id":991659,"title":"Animal wraiths","content":"It has been discussed on the Kickstarter Page 2 years ago, but since it's a thematically relevant subject;<br /> <br /> It's been confirmed that horses can become wraiths, hence giving rise to legends of the Headless Horseman of Sleepy Hollow. The image of The Charge of The Light Brigade on skeletal steeds just makes in inner gothic artist drool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And Cats, who can see into the Shadowlands unaided (like that gloriously spooky scene in Patrick Swayze's &quot;Ghost&quot;), would no doubt be spiritually aware to attain a ghostly afterlife.<br /> <br /> And then there's Ghost Dogs, like the Hound of Baskerville and the Black Dog that harry wayfarers on lonely highways.<br /> <br /> So, it seems the requirement for an animal to become a wraith seem to be:<br /> 1) Emotionally sentient<br /> 2) Have a deep emotional-connection to humans<br /> <br /> So what other animals can be found wandering the parks and zoos of Stygia? (Skeleton pigeons dropping ectoplasm on Rockerfeller and Gugenhyme playing chess in Central Park... hehehe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> If nothing else, it would be a much more stylistically vibrant underworld like The Neitherwolrld of Beetlejuice or Halloween Town! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 10-22-2016, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:34:43-07:00","id":991662,"title":"","content":"If this is true, it's a change from previously established canon. The whole point of Africa's Dark Kingdom having animal spirits was that it was a weird thing unknown anywhere else in the Underworld, and Stygia's horses had to be Moliated out of human wraiths. I'll be a little sad if this changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:33:44-07:00","id":992015,"title":"","content":"I won't <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I like the idea of Animal Wraiths. Now, can they become PCs? And could they have their own Dark Kingdoms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T00:01:50-07:00","id":992293,"title":"","content":"Was it ever confirmed what the death-steeds that Charon found were? There was a legend that they were a gift to Hades or some-such and I figure presently they were plasmics though I'd be interested to know as I found rare mention of them in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:12:09-07:00","id":992371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/991659-animal-wraiths?p=992293#post992293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it ever confirmed what the death-steeds that Charon found were? There was a legend that they were a gift to Hades or some-such and I figure presently they were plasmics though I'd be interested to know as I found rare mention of them in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I think their stats are in either <i>Ends of Empire</i> or <i>Book of Legions</i>. Pretty sure it's BoL. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:58:05-07:00","id":992930,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the horses of the Equitae are plasmics. Anyone got a page reference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:18:04-07:00","id":992958,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My books are locked up tighter than Charon's memories. Pretty sure it's the last few pages in <i>Book of Legions</i>.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:44:29-07:00","id":992965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/991659-animal-wraiths?p=992958#post992958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My books are locked up tighter than Charon's memories. Pretty sure it's the last few pages in <i>Book of Legions</i>.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. The penultimate page. But it's a tiny, tiny write-up. It doesn't explain if the steeds are Moliated or not, but the implication is that they're a unique breed of creature which can't be recreated. They're increasingly scarce, in other words, and so very unlikely to be anything as mundane as the wraiths of horses. <br /> <br /> They have all Physical Attributes at 5; Perception and Wits at 4, and Intelligence 2; Alertness, Athletics, Brawl and Dodge at 5; Intimidation 3; Argos 5; and Corpus 20. Legion policy is to save the horse and leave the wraith, if there's choice between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}